M45:lem:acyclic.statement:
[M45; research/openai_manuscript/Ambiently-homeomorphic-isolated-hypersurface-germs-in-C4-with-multiplicities-four-and-five-September-27-2026/build/sections/06-collapse.tex:12-20; lemma: inner homology and acyclic total] \label{lem:acyclic}
There are natural identifications
\begin{equation}
H_3(W)=K,\qquad H_2(W)=H/\pi_*D,\qquad
\Psi:H_3(W;\Z/k)\hookrightarrow D/kD.
\label{eq:tube-11}
\end{equation}
The large total \(\widehat\T_s\) is acyclic.

M45:lem:local.statement:
[M45; research/openai_manuscript/Ambiently-homeomorphic-isolated-hypersurface-germs-in-C4-with-multiplicities-four-and-five-September-27-2026/build/sections/06-collapse.tex:138-142; lemma: The large tube computes the local page] \label{lem:local}
The middle homology and filling pairing of the page of \eqref{eq:tube-4}
are naturally those of a sufficiently small ordinary Milnor
representative of \(f_s\).

M45:lem:mv.statement:
[M45; research/openai_manuscript/Ambiently-homeomorphic-isolated-hypersurface-germs-in-C4-with-multiplicities-four-and-five-September-27-2026/build/sections/06-collapse.tex:233-243; lemma: Mayer--Vietoris boundary] \label{lem:mv}
The full page has an exact sequence
\begin{equation}
0\longrightarrow K\longrightarrow H_3(\T_s)
\xrightarrow{\partial} H\otimes E
\xrightarrow{\overline{1\otimes\tau}}H/\pi_*D.
\label{eq:tube-13}
\end{equation}
The image of the exterior page in \(H_3(\T_s)\) maps
isomorphically under \(\partial\) to \(H\otimes\ker\tau\).

M45:eq:tube-12.statement:
[M45; research/openai_manuscript/Ambiently-homeomorphic-isolated-hypersurface-germs-in-C4-with-multiplicities-four-and-five-September-27-2026/build/sections/06-collapse.tex:43-47; equation] X(G,\D)=(G\times S^1)/
(\{g\}\times S^1\text{ collapsed for each }g\in\D).
\label{eq:tube-12}

M45:lem:bock.statement:
[M45; research/openai_manuscript/Ambiently-homeomorphic-isolated-hypersurface-germs-in-C4-with-multiplicities-four-and-five-September-27-2026/build/sections/07-lattice.tex:21-29; lemma: Bockstein equals finite-map transfer] \label{lem:bock}
For \(b\in H/kH=H_2(J)\), and any
\(\eta\in H_3(J;\Z/k)\) with \(\beta_{\rm Bock}\eta=b\),
\begin{equation}
\Psi(i_*\eta)=\pi^!b\pmod{kD},
\label{eq:tube-14}
\end{equation}
with the orientation of \(\Psi\) fixed after \eqref{eq:tube-12}.

M45:lem:inner.statement:
[M45; research/openai_manuscript/Ambiently-homeomorphic-isolated-hypersurface-germs-in-C4-with-multiplicities-four-and-five-September-27-2026/build/sections/08-fillings.tex:90-93; lemma: the inner negative sign] \label{lem:inner}
The restriction of the filling form to
\(K\) is \(-s_d|_K\).

M45:lem:arith-boundary.statement:
[M45; research/openai_manuscript/Ambiently-homeomorphic-isolated-hypersurface-germs-in-C4-with-multiplicities-four-and-five-September-27-2026/build/sections/09-arithmetic.tex:121-130; lemma: Boundary pairings] \label{lem:arith-boundary}
The classes $b_0,b_1$ are fixed by the page monodromy, and
\begin{equation}\label{eq:arith-boundary-pairings}
 \begin{aligned}
 e(b_j,b_j)&=-\frac{n_j^2}{4},&
 e(b_0,b_1)&=-\frac14,\\
 4e(b_j,x)&\equiv-\tau(x)\pmod4&&(x\in E).
 \end{aligned}
\end{equation}

M45:prop:arith-integral-congruence.statement:
[M45; research/openai_manuscript/Ambiently-homeomorphic-isolated-hypersurface-germs-in-C4-with-multiplicities-four-and-five-September-27-2026/build/sections/09-arithmetic.tex:556-560; proposition: Integral Seifert congruence] \label{prop:arith-integral-congruence}
For the two germs constructed above, the two integral Milnor Seifert
forms $(\Lambda_0,s_0)$ and $(\Lambda_1,s_1)$ are isometric.

